WEBVTT

00:00.350 --> 00:05.709
Your code needs to save a draft. An effect declares the need. Your function asks for it.

00:06.109 --> 00:08.810
Choose the disk handler, and the draft is saved.

00:09.210 --> 00:14.048
Choose the offline handler, and test the failure. Same function. Different world.

00:14.448 --> 00:21.447
Three uncompromising flavors: Default, ML, and Python. No lock-in. Mix them in one project.

00:21.847 --> 00:31.199
Bring your Python thinking to Osprey. Our GPT-2 port runs on the CPU or GPU. The handler decides where the arithmetic runs.

00:31.599 --> 00:36.207
Try Osprey in your browser. Open source, actively evolving. Logic, in flight.
